<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<!--
  folio-assistant — Editing subprocess — evidence for a recommendation.

  STRAWPERSON. The shape is real and renders; the concrete registry list, the
  grading system and the API bindings are deliberately NOT fixed here; a
  separate process refines them.

  Source of truth: this file. Open it in bpmn.io, Camunda Modeler, or any other
  BPMN 2.0 tool. The SVG under docs/assets/img/workflows/ is generated from it
  by `bun run cat render:bpmn` — never hand-edit the SVG.

  The <bootstrap.processes:skill> extension on an activity names the folio-assistant skill
  that implements it; <cat-harness.processes:bean> marks a step that reads or writes the shared
  work plan in beans/.
-->
<bpmn:definitions xmlns:bpmn="http://www.omg.org/spec/BPMN/20100524/MODEL"
                  xmlns:bpmndi="http://www.omg.org/spec/BPMN/20100524/DI"
                  xmlns:dc="http://www.omg.org/spec/DD/20100524/DC"
                  xmlns:di="http://www.omg.org/spec/DD/20100524/DI"
                  xmlns:bootstrap.processes="https://litlfred.github.io/bootstrap/v0/processes/ns/"
                  xmlns:cat-harness.processes="https://litlfred.github.io/cat-harness/v0/processes/ns/"
                  id="Definitions_EvidenceRetrieval"
                  targetNamespace="https://litlfred.github.io/folio-assistant/workflows"
                  exporter="folio-assistant" exporterVersion="1">
  <bpmn:import namespace="https://litlfred.github.io/bootstrap/v0/processes/ns/" location="https://litlfred.github.io/bootstrap/v0/processes/ns.jsonld" importType="http://www.w3.org/ns/json-ld"/>
  <bpmn:resource id="author" name="Author"/>
  <bpmn:resource id="evidence-agent" name="Evidence agent"/>
  <bpmn:resource id="external-registry" name="External registry"/>
  <bpmn:resource id="work-plan" name="Work plan (beans)"/>
  <bpmn:collaboration id="Collaboration_EvidenceRetrieval">
    <bpmn:participant id="Participant_EvidenceRetrieval" name="Editing subprocess — evidence for a recommendation" processRef="Process_EvidenceRetrieval" />
  </bpmn:collaboration>
  <bpmn:process id="Process_EvidenceRetrieval" name="Evidence for a recommendation" isExecutable="false">
    <bpmn:documentation>Frame a question for a recommendation, retrieve and appraise evidence from trusted sources, and either attach it or record the gap; a change that states or alters no recommendation ends at its own event before any search. Evidence comes from three classes (trusted L1 sources, trusted L2/L3 content, data repositories), and each candidate's authority is verified against the publishing body's own API. STRAWPERSON: registries, grading system and API bindings are not fixed here.</bpmn:documentation>
    <bpmn:laneSet id="LaneSet_EvidenceRetrieval">
      <bpmn:lane id="Lane_Author" name="Author / guideline developer (person)" partitionElementRef="author">
        <bpmn:documentation>Brackets the machine work rather than doing it: frames the PICO before Lane_Agent fans out across evidence classes, then is the only lane that grades what comes back and decides whether it is sufficient for a recommendation; retrieval and authority-checking are delegated.</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>StartEvent_Recommendation</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>Gateway_RecommendationInPlay</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>EndEvent_NoRecommendation</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>Task_ReviewExisting</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>Task_FramePico</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>Task_AppraiseGrade</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>Gateway_Sufficient</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>Task_AttachEvidence</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>EndEvent_EvidenceAttached</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>Task_RecordUnverified</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>Task_RecordGap</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>EndEvent_GapRecorded</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
      </bpmn:lane>
      <bpmn:lane id="Lane_Agent" name="Evidence agent (system)" partitionElementRef="evidence-agent">
        <bpmn:documentation>Fans out in parallel across the three evidence classes and joins the candidates. It owns coverage, not judgement: grading is Lane_Author's call and authority is Lane_Trusted's.</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>Gateway_RetrievalFork</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>Task_L1Sources</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>Task_L2L3Content</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>Task_DataRepos</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>Gateway_RetrievalJoin</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
      </bpmn:lane>
      <bpmn:lane id="Lane_Trusted" name="Trusted registries and observatories (external)" partitionElementRef="external-registry">
        <bpmn:documentation>Task_VerifyAuthority and its gateway sit here rather than with Lane_Agent because the decision is a readout of what the external API returns, not this instance's call; when that answer is uncertain or absent, a bean is opened rather than a verdict invented.</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>Task_VerifyAuthority</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>Gateway_Authoritative</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
      </bpmn:lane>
    </bpmn:laneSet>
    <bpmn:startEvent id="StartEvent_Recommendation" name="An edit is about to be drafted">
      <bpmn:outgoing>Flow_01</bpmn:outgoing>
    </bpmn:startEvent>
    <bpmn:exclusiveGateway id="Gateway_RecommendationInPlay" name="Does the change state or alter a recommendation?">
      <bpmn:documentation>The author answers before any search starts. `yes`: the change states a recommendation or alters one, and the evidence is gathered as below. `no`: the change carries none -- a mathematics folio has none, and a figure redrawn from its own source as a computable graphic adds or changes none -- so there is nothing to frame as PICO. The `no` branch ends at its own event, which records that answer in the instance history; it does not pretend a search was run. The answer is the author's and the editor still rules on the change at Task_ReviewFindings in Process_Editing, so a wrong `no` is caught there.</bpmn:documentation>
      <bpmn:incoming>Flow_01</bpmn:incoming>
      <bpmn:outgoing>Flow_RecYes</bpmn:outgoing>
      <bpmn:outgoing>Flow_RecNo</bpmn:outgoing>
    </bpmn:exclusiveGateway>
    <bpmn:endEvent id="EndEvent_NoRecommendation" name="No recommendation in this change">
      <bpmn:incoming>Flow_RecNo</bpmn:incoming>
    </bpmn:endEvent>
    <bpmn:userTask id="Task_ReviewExisting" name="Review the existing guidance">
      <bpmn:documentation>The author reads what the document, DAK or IG ALREADY says on this question, before looking outward. A recommendation that contradicts a sibling recommendation in the same artefact is a defect no external evidence will reveal.</bpmn:documentation>
      <bpmn:extensionElements>
        <bootstrap.processes:skill ref="content-review" />
      </bpmn:extensionElements>
      <bpmn:incoming>Flow_RecYes</bpmn:incoming>
      <bpmn:outgoing>Flow_02</bpmn:outgoing>
    </bpmn:userTask>
    <bpmn:userTask id="Task_FramePico" name="Frame the question as PICO">
      <bpmn:documentation>Population, Intervention, Comparator, Outcome. The PICO is what makes the search reproducible and the evidence auditable: without it, 'we looked for evidence' is not a claim anyone can check. WHO guideline development states the question this way before any retrieval.</bpmn:documentation>
      <bpmn:extensionElements>
        <bootstrap.processes:skill ref="content-author" />
      </bpmn:extensionElements>
      <bpmn:incoming>Flow_02</bpmn:incoming>
      <bpmn:outgoing>Flow_03</bpmn:outgoing>
    </bpmn:userTask>
    <bpmn:parallelGateway id="Gateway_RetrievalFork" name="Retrieve across evidence classes">
      <bpmn:incoming>Flow_03</bpmn:incoming>
      <bpmn:outgoing>Flow_04</bpmn:outgoing>
      <bpmn:outgoing>Flow_05</bpmn:outgoing>
      <bpmn:outgoing>Flow_06</bpmn:outgoing>
    </bpmn:parallelGateway>
    <bpmn:serviceTask id="Task_L1Sources" name="Search trusted L1 sources">
      <bpmn:documentation>Ingested primary literature under library/: the sections/*.md tree and, where a document was scanned, ocr/page-NNN.txt. NOTE the known blind spot — a document OCR'd but never re-run through pdf-structure.py has only a stub in sections/, so a sections-only search misses it.</bpmn:documentation>
      <bpmn:extensionElements>
        <bootstrap.processes:skill ref="document-intake" />
      </bpmn:extensionElements>
      <bpmn:incoming>Flow_04</bpmn:incoming>
      <bpmn:outgoing>Flow_07</bpmn:outgoing>
    </bpmn:serviceTask>
    <bpmn:serviceTask id="Task_L2L3Content" name="Search trusted L2 and L3 content">
      <bpmn:documentation>Already-adjudicated guidance: WHO SMART DAKs at L2 and FHIR Implementation Guides at L3. A recommendation adopted in a published DAK is evidence of a different kind from a primary study -- it is a prior decision, with its own provenance, and must be cited as that rather than laundered into primary evidence.

NOT YET SKILL-BACKED: no skill searches adjudicated L2/L3 content for
evidence. `corpus-grep` is a different task (checking that a gap is really
open).</bpmn:documentation>
      <bpmn:extensionElements>
        <bootstrap.processes:skill ref="document-intake" />
        <bootstrap.processes:skill ref="document-intake" />
        <bootstrap.processes:skill ref="document-intake" />
      </bpmn:extensionElements>
      <bpmn:incoming>Flow_05</bpmn:incoming>
      <bpmn:outgoing>Flow_08</bpmn:outgoing>
    </bpmn:serviceTask>
    <bpmn:serviceTask id="Task_DataRepos" name="Query data repositories and statistical datasets">
      <bpmn:documentation>Indicator and microdata sources. Distinct from the two above because the unit of evidence is a MEASUREMENT with a population, a period and a method, not a claim in prose.</bpmn:documentation>
      <bpmn:extensionElements>
        <bootstrap.processes:skill ref="document-intake" />
        <bootstrap.processes:skill ref="document-intake" />
        <bootstrap.processes:skill ref="document-intake" />
      </bpmn:extensionElements>
      <bpmn:incoming>Flow_06</bpmn:incoming>
      <bpmn:outgoing>Flow_09</bpmn:outgoing>
    </bpmn:serviceTask>
    <bpmn:parallelGateway id="Gateway_RetrievalJoin" name="Candidates assembled">
      <bpmn:incoming>Flow_07</bpmn:incoming>
      <bpmn:incoming>Flow_08</bpmn:incoming>
      <bpmn:incoming>Flow_09</bpmn:incoming>
      <bpmn:outgoing>Flow_10</bpmn:outgoing>
    </bpmn:parallelGateway>
    <bpmn:serviceTask id="Task_VerifyAuthority" name="Verify authority against the registry">
      <bpmn:documentation>Each candidate is resolved against the standard API of the body that publishes it, so that 'authoritative' is a RESOLVED FACT rather than an assertion in the citation. What is checked: that the identifier resolves at the publisher; that the retrieved record matches what the citation claims; that the version and date are the ones cited; and that the publisher is one this folio has declared trusted. STRAWPERSON: the concrete registry list and endpoints are not settled here -- see the cat-harness.processes:policy note.</bpmn:documentation>
      <bpmn:extensionElements>
        <cat-harness.processes:policy enforcement="strict" />
        <bootstrap.processes:skill ref="registry-authority-contract" />
      </bpmn:extensionElements>
      <bpmn:incoming>Flow_10</bpmn:incoming>
      <bpmn:outgoing>Flow_11</bpmn:outgoing>
    </bpmn:serviceTask>
    <bpmn:exclusiveGateway id="Gateway_Authoritative" name="Authority confirmed?">
      <bpmn:documentation>Answered by checking the source against the observatory or registry API: is its authority confirmed? `no` opens a bean for the unverified citation; `yes` goes on to appraise and grade the evidence.</bpmn:documentation>
      <bpmn:incoming>Flow_11</bpmn:incoming>
      <bpmn:outgoing>Flow_12</bpmn:outgoing>
      <bpmn:outgoing>Flow_13</bpmn:outgoing>
    </bpmn:exclusiveGateway>
    <bpmn:serviceTask id="Task_RecordUnverified" name="Open a bean for the unverified citation">
      <bpmn:documentation>An unresolvable citation is not dropped and not silently kept. It becomes a tracked item, so the gap is visible in the work plan rather than surviving as a footnote nobody re-checks.</bpmn:documentation>
      <bpmn:extensionElements>
        <bootstrap.processes:skill ref="todo-manager" />
        <cat-harness.processes:bean op="note" />
      </bpmn:extensionElements>
      <bpmn:incoming>Flow_12</bpmn:incoming>
      <bpmn:outgoing>Flow_14</bpmn:outgoing>
      <bpmn:dataOutputAssociation id="DOA_Task_RecordUnverified">
        <bpmn:targetRef>DSR_work_plan</bpmn:targetRef>
      </bpmn:dataOutputAssociation>
    </bpmn:serviceTask>
    <bpmn:userTask id="Task_AppraiseGrade" name="Appraise and grade the body of evidence">
      <bpmn:documentation>Certainty of evidence per the grading system the folio declares. The grade attaches to the BODY of evidence for one PICO question, not to an individual citation -- which is why this step is after the join and not inside the fan-out.</bpmn:documentation>
      <bpmn:extensionElements>
        <bootstrap.processes:skill ref="evidence-appraisal" />
      </bpmn:extensionElements>
      <bpmn:incoming>Flow_13</bpmn:incoming>
      <bpmn:incoming>Flow_14</bpmn:incoming>
      <bpmn:outgoing>Flow_15</bpmn:outgoing>
    </bpmn:userTask>
    <bpmn:exclusiveGateway id="Gateway_Sufficient" name="Sufficient for a recommendation?">
      <bpmn:documentation>Answered by the appraisal: is the graded evidence enough to support a recommendation? `no` records the evidence gap; `yes` attaches the evidence to the recommendation.</bpmn:documentation>
      <bpmn:incoming>Flow_15</bpmn:incoming>
      <bpmn:outgoing>Flow_16</bpmn:outgoing>
      <bpmn:outgoing>Flow_17</bpmn:outgoing>
    </bpmn:exclusiveGateway>
    <bpmn:serviceTask id="Task_RecordGap" name="Record the evidence gap">
      <bpmn:documentation>Insufficient evidence is a RESULT. It is recorded as such -- an honest gap the guideline can state -- rather than being closed by weakening the recommendation until the available evidence supports it.</bpmn:documentation>
      <bpmn:extensionElements>
        <bootstrap.processes:skill ref="todo-manager" />
        <cat-harness.processes:bean op="note" />
      </bpmn:extensionElements>
      <bpmn:incoming>Flow_16</bpmn:incoming>
      <bpmn:outgoing>Flow_18</bpmn:outgoing>
      <bpmn:dataOutputAssociation id="DOA_Task_RecordGap">
        <bpmn:targetRef>DSR_work_plan</bpmn:targetRef>
      </bpmn:dataOutputAssociation>
    </bpmn:serviceTask>
    <bpmn:userTask id="Task_AttachEvidence" name="Attach the evidence">
      <bpmn:documentation>The PICO, the graded body of evidence, each verified citation and its resolved authority record are written onto the recommendation block, so a reader can retrace the whole chain from the sentence back to the source.</bpmn:documentation>
      <bpmn:extensionElements>
        <bootstrap.processes:skill ref="content-author" />
      </bpmn:extensionElements>
      <bpmn:incoming>Flow_17</bpmn:incoming>
      <bpmn:outgoing>Flow_19</bpmn:outgoing>
    </bpmn:userTask>
    <bpmn:endEvent id="EndEvent_EvidenceAttached" name="Recommendation is evidence-backed">
      <bpmn:incoming>Flow_19</bpmn:incoming>
    </bpmn:endEvent>
    <bpmn:endEvent id="EndEvent_GapRecorded" name="Gap recorded, no recommendation">
      <bpmn:incoming>Flow_18</bpmn:incoming>
    </bpmn:endEvent>
    <bpmn:sequenceFlow id="Flow_01" sourceRef="StartEvent_Recommendation" targetRef="Gateway_RecommendationInPlay" />
    <bpmn:sequenceFlow id="Flow_RecYes" name="yes" sourceRef="Gateway_RecommendationInPlay" targetRef="Task_ReviewExisting" />
    <bpmn:sequenceFlow id="Flow_RecNo" name="no" sourceRef="Gateway_RecommendationInPlay" targetRef="EndEvent_NoRecommendation" />
    <bpmn:sequenceFlow id="Flow_02" sourceRef="Task_ReviewExisting" targetRef="Task_FramePico" />
    <bpmn:sequenceFlow id="Flow_03" sourceRef="Task_FramePico" targetRef="Gateway_RetrievalFork" />
    <bpmn:sequenceFlow id="Flow_04" sourceRef="Gateway_RetrievalFork" targetRef="Task_L1Sources" />
    <bpmn:sequenceFlow id="Flow_05" sourceRef="Gateway_RetrievalFork" targetRef="Task_L2L3Content" />
    <bpmn:sequenceFlow id="Flow_06" sourceRef="Gateway_RetrievalFork" targetRef="Task_DataRepos" />
    <bpmn:sequenceFlow id="Flow_07" sourceRef="Task_L1Sources" targetRef="Gateway_RetrievalJoin" />
    <bpmn:sequenceFlow id="Flow_08" sourceRef="Task_L2L3Content" targetRef="Gateway_RetrievalJoin" />
    <bpmn:sequenceFlow id="Flow_09" sourceRef="Task_DataRepos" targetRef="Gateway_RetrievalJoin" />
    <bpmn:sequenceFlow id="Flow_10" sourceRef="Gateway_RetrievalJoin" targetRef="Task_VerifyAuthority" />
    <bpmn:sequenceFlow id="Flow_11" sourceRef="Task_VerifyAuthority" targetRef="Gateway_Authoritative" />
    <bpmn:sequenceFlow id="Flow_12" name="no" sourceRef="Gateway_Authoritative" targetRef="Task_RecordUnverified" />
    <bpmn:sequenceFlow id="Flow_13" name="yes" sourceRef="Gateway_Authoritative" targetRef="Task_AppraiseGrade" />
    <bpmn:sequenceFlow id="Flow_14" sourceRef="Task_RecordUnverified" targetRef="Task_AppraiseGrade" />
    <bpmn:sequenceFlow id="Flow_15" sourceRef="Task_AppraiseGrade" targetRef="Gateway_Sufficient" />
    <bpmn:sequenceFlow id="Flow_16" name="no" sourceRef="Gateway_Sufficient" targetRef="Task_RecordGap" />
    <bpmn:sequenceFlow id="Flow_17" name="yes" sourceRef="Gateway_Sufficient" targetRef="Task_AttachEvidence" />
    <bpmn:sequenceFlow id="Flow_18" sourceRef="Task_RecordGap" targetRef="EndEvent_GapRecorded" />
    <bpmn:sequenceFlow id="Flow_19" sourceRef="Task_AttachEvidence" targetRef="EndEvent_EvidenceAttached" />
    <bpmn:dataStoreReference id="DSR_work_plan" name="Work plan (beans)" dataStoreRef="work-plan"/>
  </bpmn:process>
  <bpmndi:BPMNDiagram id="Diagram_EvidenceRetrieval">
    <bpmndi:BPMNPlane id="Plane_EvidenceRetrieval" bpmnElement="Collaboration_EvidenceRetrieval">
      <bpmndi:BPMNShape id="Participant_EvidenceRetrieval_di" bpmnElement="Participant_EvidenceRetrieval" isHorizontal="true"><dc:Bounds x="160" y="80" width="2765" height="767" /></bpmndi:BPMNShape>
      <bpmndi:BPMNShape id="Lane_Author_di" bpmnElement="Lane_Author" isHorizontal="true"><dc:Bounds x="190" y="440" width="2735" height="407" /></bpmndi:BPMNShape>
      <bpmndi:BPMNShape id="Lane_Agent_di" bpmnElement="Lane_Agent" isHorizontal="true"><dc:Bounds x="190" y="260" width="2735" height="180" /></bpmndi:BPMNShape>
      <bpmndi:BPMNShape id="Lane_Trusted_di" bpmnElement="Lane_Trusted" isHorizontal="true"><dc:Bounds x="190" y="80" width="2735" height="180" /></bpmndi:BPMNShape>

      <bpmndi:BPMNShape id="StartEvent_Recommendation_di" bpmnElement="StartEvent_Recommendation"><dc:Bounds x="237" y="512" width="36" height="36" />
        <bpmndi:BPMNLabel><dc:Bounds x="218.01" y="547.5" width="90" height="53" /></bpmndi:BPMNLabel>
      </bpmndi:BPMNShape>
      <bpmndi:BPMNShape id="Gateway_RecommendationInPlay_di" bpmnElement="Gateway_RecommendationInPlay" isMarkerVisible="true"><dc:Bounds x="320" y="505" width="50" height="50" />
        <bpmndi:BPMNLabel><dc:Bounds x="255" y="447" width="180" height="54" /></bpmndi:BPMNLabel>
      </bpmndi:BPMNShape>
      <bpmndi:BPMNShape id="EndEvent_NoRecommendation_di" bpmnElement="EndEvent_NoRecommendation"><dc:Bounds x="327" y="605" width="36" height="36" />
        <bpmndi:BPMNLabel><dc:Bounds x="370" y="603" width="110" height="40" /></bpmndi:BPMNLabel>
      </bpmndi:BPMNShape>
      <bpmndi:BPMNShape id="Task_ReviewExisting_di" bpmnElement="Task_ReviewExisting"><dc:Bounds x="445" y="470" width="120" height="120" /></bpmndi:BPMNShape>
      <bpmndi:BPMNShape id="Task_FramePico_di" bpmnElement="Task_FramePico"><dc:Bounds x="665" y="470" width="120" height="120" /></bpmndi:BPMNShape>
      <bpmndi:BPMNShape id="Gateway_RetrievalFork_di" bpmnElement="Gateway_RetrievalFork"><dc:Bounds x="880" y="325" width="50" height="50" />
        
      <bpmndi:BPMNLabel><dc:Bounds x="741" y="267" width="135" height="54" /></bpmndi:BPMNLabel></bpmndi:BPMNShape>
      <bpmndi:BPMNShape id="Task_L1Sources_di" bpmnElement="Task_L1Sources"><dc:Bounds x="1035" y="555" width="120" height="120" /></bpmndi:BPMNShape>
      <bpmndi:BPMNShape id="Task_L2L3Content_di" bpmnElement="Task_L2L3Content"><dc:Bounds x="1035" y="290" width="120" height="120" /></bpmndi:BPMNShape>
      <bpmndi:BPMNShape id="Task_DataRepos_di" bpmnElement="Task_DataRepos"><dc:Bounds x="1035" y="92" width="120" height="120" /></bpmndi:BPMNShape>
      <bpmndi:BPMNShape id="Gateway_RetrievalJoin_di" bpmnElement="Gateway_RetrievalJoin"><dc:Bounds x="1240" y="325" width="50" height="50" /></bpmndi:BPMNShape>
      <bpmndi:BPMNShape id="Task_VerifyAuthority_di" bpmnElement="Task_VerifyAuthority"><dc:Bounds x="1425" y="110" width="120" height="120" /></bpmndi:BPMNShape>
      <bpmndi:BPMNShape id="Gateway_Authoritative_di" bpmnElement="Gateway_Authoritative" isMarkerVisible="true"><dc:Bounds x="1620" y="145" width="50" height="50" /></bpmndi:BPMNShape>
      <bpmndi:BPMNShape id="Task_RecordUnverified_di" bpmnElement="Task_RecordUnverified"><dc:Bounds x="1755" y="706.5" width="180" height="101" /></bpmndi:BPMNShape>
      <bpmndi:BPMNShape id="Task_AppraiseGrade_di" bpmnElement="Task_AppraiseGrade"><dc:Bounds x="1925" y="470" width="120" height="120" /></bpmndi:BPMNShape>
      <bpmndi:BPMNShape id="Gateway_Sufficient_di" bpmnElement="Gateway_Sufficient" isMarkerVisible="true"><dc:Bounds x="2120" y="505" width="50" height="50" /></bpmndi:BPMNShape>
      <bpmndi:BPMNShape id="Task_RecordGap_di" bpmnElement="Task_RecordGap"><dc:Bounds x="2255" y="706.5" width="180" height="101" /></bpmndi:BPMNShape>
      <bpmndi:BPMNShape id="Task_AttachEvidence_di" bpmnElement="Task_AttachEvidence"><dc:Bounds x="2425" y="470" width="120" height="120" /></bpmndi:BPMNShape>
      <bpmndi:BPMNShape id="EndEvent_EvidenceAttached_di" bpmnElement="EndEvent_EvidenceAttached"><dc:Bounds x="2645" y="512" width="36" height="36" /></bpmndi:BPMNShape>
      <bpmndi:BPMNShape id="EndEvent_GapRecorded_di" bpmnElement="EndEvent_GapRecorded"><dc:Bounds x="2445" y="739" width="36" height="36" />
        
      <bpmndi:BPMNLabel><dc:Bounds x="2485" y="712.5" width="90" height="89" /></bpmndi:BPMNLabel></bpmndi:BPMNShape>
      <bpmndi:BPMNEdge id="Flow_01_di" bpmnElement="Flow_01">
        <di:waypoint x="273" y="530" />
        <di:waypoint x="320" y="530" />
      </bpmndi:BPMNEdge>
      <bpmndi:BPMNEdge id="Flow_RecYes_di" bpmnElement="Flow_RecYes">
        <di:waypoint x="370" y="530" />
        <di:waypoint x="445" y="530" />
        <bpmndi:BPMNLabel><dc:Bounds x="380" y="512" width="20" height="14" /></bpmndi:BPMNLabel>
      </bpmndi:BPMNEdge>
      <bpmndi:BPMNEdge id="Flow_RecNo_di" bpmnElement="Flow_RecNo">
        <di:waypoint x="345" y="555" />
        <di:waypoint x="345" y="605" />
        <bpmndi:BPMNLabel><dc:Bounds x="350" y="570" width="20" height="14" /></bpmndi:BPMNLabel>
      </bpmndi:BPMNEdge>
      <bpmndi:BPMNEdge id="Flow_02_di" bpmnElement="Flow_02">
        <di:waypoint x="565" y="530" />
        <di:waypoint x="665" y="530" />
